<DocsLayout title="First boot">
    <h1>First boot</h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        A few useful steps after starting your newly installed Octlitch system.
    </p>

    <h2>Update the system</h2>

    <p>
        Start by installing the latest Fedora package updates.
    </p>

    <pre><code>sudo dnf upgrade --refresh</code></pre>

    <p>
        Restart the system if the update includes important system
        components such as the kernel, systemd or graphics libraries.
    </p>

    <h2>Install applications</h2>

    <p>
        Octlitch uses two primary application sources.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>DNF</strong> for operating system packages and system
            components.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Flatpak and Flathub</strong> for many desktop applications.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        KDE Discover is included as the graphical application manager for
        Flatpak applications.
    </p>

    <h2>Choose an Octlitch theme</h2>

    <p>
        Octlitch includes four curated desktop looks:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Valley</li>
        <li>Model</li>
        <li>Coast</li>
        <li>Mountain</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        They can be selected from KDE Plasma's appearance settings.
    </p>

    <h2>NVIDIA graphics</h2>

    <p>
        Proprietary NVIDIA drivers are intentionally not included in the
        installation image.
    </p>

    <p>
        Octlitch provides a post-install helper for users who choose to
        install the NVIDIA driver:
    </p>

    <pre><code>sudo octlitch-install-nvidia</code></pre>

    <p>
        See the NVIDIA chapter for details, including Secure Boot
        considerations.
    </p>

    <h2>Need help?</h2>

    <p>
        Continue through the handbook for package management, hardware,
        gaming and troubleshooting information.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-next">
        <a href="/documentation/packages/dnf/">
            Next: DNF package management →
        </a>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
